          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_710da5d5ac8a",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_af8f1fbfe191",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_55ec68a77a25",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        }
      ],
      "focus": "Examine Region A's material and territorial scope; treatment processing by registered health professionals; the treatment of identified genetic, health, and identity information; consent requirements; any impact-assessment requirements; and the outward-transfer framework, including recognition, approved clauses, and specific-situation derogations. Delegate to Subregion A1 for its health-information, genetic-information, professional-secrecy, and outward-transfer provisions."
    },
    {
      "corpus": "region_b",
      "engaged": true,
      "reason": "The recipient is established in Region B, the referral documents will be uploaded to and stored in B, and the Region B clinic will access and use the health records for its own treatment of the patient. Region B therefore has a direct territorial connection to the receipt, clinical use, security, retention, and possible access or disclosure of the records.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact_id": "f_7f9bd01bdf80",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_c345501e8bd4",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_5aa17aaaa329",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_73d3eb94625a",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_a7a94423ed89",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_3707d0e0f8a9",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_8c44c6e413c5",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f_febc895bce9e",
          "path": "",
          "quote": ""
        }
      ],
      "focus": "Examine whether the Region B Health Records Act applies to a private specialist clinic receiving identified genetic and health records for its own treatment; permitted use or disclosure for the second opinion and video consultation; minimum-necessary handling; security of the encrypted portal; retention in the clinic's own record; and any relevance of the absence of Trusted Recipient Scheme certification. Also assess any Region B Records Access Act provisions concerning production, non-disclosure, encryption, or review."
    }
  ]
}

